to make it to the store again this week.\h\h
Also, civil servant exam cram sessions are starting soon,\h
so I'll be focusing on my studies for a while.
I may have to quit my job.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.670
Welcome home, Seigi.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:32.160
I had no idea you had such a cute girlfriend.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:36.010
She's not my girlfriend. 
She's just an acquaintance.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.560
It's none of your business.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.690
Wait! Where are you going?

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.390
<b>Housewares

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.140
Come on, you don't need to go shopping.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.020
Let's go someplace to eat, Seigi.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.900
Your old man's hungry.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.100
Have you ever wanted to die?

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.400
What? Die?

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.130
I have.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:55.890
I wanted to kill you, and then kill myself.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:01.320
Wait, Seigi. Why are you so mad?

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.800
How did you get my address?

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:08.370
I, uh, just happened to find it.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.860
I guess we really do share 
a bond as father and son.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:15.470
There's nothing between you and me!

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.640
You have twenty seconds to disappear.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.390
Why are you being so mean?

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:30.110
You're making your old man sad.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:34.180
Twenty, nineteen...

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:34.180
I've always loved you.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:37.410
When did you grow up to be a bad boy?

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:38.620
Eighteen, seventeen...

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:41.520
Listen, Seigi. Hear me out.

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:42.310
Sixteen, fifteen...

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.120
The bill collectors showed up.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.580
Fourteen, thirteen...

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.460
I'm telling you to listen!

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:50.710
Twelve, eleven...

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.710
Keep treating your father like this, 
and you'll pay for it!

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:51.930
Ten...

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:56.680
Nine... eight...

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:57.930
Seigi... You know what's really interesting?

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:07.050
Seven... six... five... four...

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:05.010
You may not have noticed, but you're 
becoming more and more like me.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.810
You really are my son.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:08.770
Three...

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:13.110
You might think you're hiding it, 
but it's no use.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:16.640
You'll end up just like me.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:31.060
Seigi, why?

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:48.380
Keep treating your father like this, 
and you'll pay for it!

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:47.460
Eleven...

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:54.230
Ten... nine... eight...

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:55.650
Damn it!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.290
Number Withheld

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:06.870
Who's this?

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:12.690
<i>Hello, Seigi? You home right now?</i>

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:15.610
<i>I'm on my way over. 
Leave the door unlocked.</i>

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.490
I've been expecting you.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:46.490
Thank you for contacting me.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.590
It's been a while, Seigi.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:58.250
Sorry for bothering you.

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:02.080
You can make up for it by working for me.

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:03.510
About that...

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:08.770
I'm sure you've heard from Saul-san, 
but I'm busy with my studies.

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:10.190
Yes.

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:12.850
I want to quit as of today.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.610
I see. Very well.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:16.820
Huh?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:21.880
Then I suppose this will be our last day 
working together in the store.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:25.030
I suppose it will.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:28.290
I look forward to one more day with you.

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:31.540
M-Me, too.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:39.120
Tanzanite is a blue zoisite from Tanzania.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:44.620
With its mystical color and 
easy-to-remember name, it's quite popular.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:49.190
Because its color is reminiscent 
of the pre-dawn sky,

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:55.310
it's thought to help people inhabit new lives...
In other words, it signifies rebirth.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.130
Rebirth, huh?

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:00.920
When I was a child, 
I wanted to become an adventurer.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:03.220
But if I were reborn now,

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:05.820
I'd like to work in a gemstone-related 
profession like you.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.270
You intend to become my business rival?

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.330
Go easy on me.

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:14.830
Nakata-kun, if you could be reborn, 
what would you want to be?

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.590
What? Me?

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:22.590
I'd like to be... anyone who isn't me.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.350
What's the matter, Nakata-kun?

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.410
Huh? Uh...

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:29.260
You okay? Feeling a little tired?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.560
Regarding the earlier question...

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:42.440
If I were reborn, 
I would want to be someone like you.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:43.320
Huh?

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:47.350
Just as you released me 
from that detestable will,

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:50.830
if you're ever in trouble, 
I'd like to be the one

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:57.080
traveling to the ends 
of the earth to help you.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:04.390
Those words alone will keep me 
going for the rest of my life.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:10.880
Richard.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:15.770
I may not have worked here long,
but thank you for everything.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.520
Before you go, 
there's something I'd like to discuss.

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:23.650
Shimeno Hisashi is a troublesome man.

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:33.790
Richard, you...

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:38.360
You were acting strange, 
so I had Jeffrey look into it.

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:42.130
Remember, you flew to London 
without saying anything to me.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:44.300
Yeah, but...

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:47.450
Why didn't you tell me?

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:51.570
There are some things I can't tell you...

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:56.680
I could say the same thing to you, 
who chased me all the way to London.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:00.950
There are some things in this world 
we can't do anything about.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:04.500
How did you respond when I said that to you?

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.320
Well...

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:09.250
If you won't say it, then allow me.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:14.420
Seigi, do you intend to carry 
all your burdens alone?

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:19.930
Why must you treat me like some 
stone cast by the roadside?

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:22.340
Who do you think I am?

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:29.800
Because I love you so much, 
I'm equally as angry with you.

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:34.290
I've lived longer than you have.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:37.000
I know more than you do.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:43.340
But you left me behind and went 
on to walk into darkness alone.

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:44.540
Why?

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:51.970
If he knew I continued working here,
 he'd come around to mooch money off of you.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:55.330
He'd say a child's money 
belongs to their parents.

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.970
That's just the kind of guy he is.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:15:02.280
Once he figures out where you live, 
he'll pester you until you leave.

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:07.830
And you hid this even from your 
mother in order to avoid that?

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:14.800
I don't want to trouble you 
or Hiromi over this.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:19.730
I appreciate the thought, but you 
need only take appropriate measures.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:24.710
What's the real reason you want 
to quit working at Étranger, Seigi?

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:35.300
I... almost stabbed him the other day.

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:41.160
If he hadn't backed off, 
I might've actually done it.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.310
I'm sure I've lost your respect...

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:48.630
I may hide it from you, 
but I'm actually a hopeless person.

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:58.290
Thank you for telling me, Seigi.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.140
Huh?

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:02.530
In spite of that, you didn't lose your way.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:06.150
I admire that about you.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:11.560
You mean... you haven't lost respect for me?

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:15.800
If anything, shouldn't I applaud
the strength you've demonstrated

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.680
by facing your own weakness?

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:20.040
I have no strength...

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:23.500
I know better than you do 
just how strong you are.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:31.000
You're bursting with not just strength,
 but also kindness.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.140
You're a truly strong person.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:37.560
But his blood flows inside me.

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.520
I'm afraid of myself.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:45.060
Then why not carry that weakness with you?

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:46.350
Huh?

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:49.570
You can only run from someone 
who won't listen to you.

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:53.280
And that's coming from someone who's 
been running from his own family,

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.570
so you know it's true.

00:16:57.810 --> 00:17:00.140
Believe in yourself, Seigi.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:02.540
You're not alone.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:07.280
I'm... not alone.

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:10.670
What should I have done?

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:15.120
Whether choosing to run or to confront him, 
you should've asked for help.

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:17.760
All right.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:20.560
Now, turn on your phone.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:21.260
What?

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:23.890
It's all right. I'm here for you.

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:47.630
Oh? So you're an acquaintance of Seigi's, huh?

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:51.210
I'm his father. Thanks for looking after him.

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:55.560
What a strange thing to say.

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:57.290
What's strange about that?

00:17:57.290 --> 00:18:02.470
As far as I'm aware, Seigi only has one father.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.530
What?

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:04.720
Hello.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:07.980
Who are you?

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:09.730
I'm Seigi's father.

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:10.980
What?

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.940
Nakata-san?! Why...

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:18.570
Please stop following my son around.

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:22.680
Oh, right. You're the guy Hiromi married.

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:26.040
Well, I'm still Seigi's father by blood.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.140
If you're his father, then answer me this.

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:35.020
Do you know how Seigi placed in his 
sixth grade relay race on field day?

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.210
What?

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.000
When is his birthday?

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.910
What's his favorite food? 
His favorite sport?

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:44.930
What was the name of the teacher 
Seigi was closest to in middle school?

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:47.860
I know all of that.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.690
S-So what?

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:55.440
We may not be related by blood, 
but Seigi is my beloved son!

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:00.700
Anyone who bothers him deals with <i>me</i>.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.090
So leave him alone.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:09.600
Don't you realize you can't sever
 the bond between father and son?

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:13.670
Seigi! Seigi, tell him!

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:14.840
Seigi...

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:19.690
I'm not Shimeno Seigi. I'm Nakata Seigi.

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:21.890
I'll never be like you.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:24.760
Seigi...

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.160
What are you talking about, Seigi?

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:29.360
Even if you can't sever 
the father-and-son bond,

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:33.130
there are legal methods 
to keep you at a distance.

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.980
Wouldn't you prefer to avoid all that trouble?

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:39.150
Or shall we go to the police?

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:42.660
Damn it.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:57.390
Nakata-san, how did...

00:19:57.390 --> 00:20:00.090
Richard-san contacted me.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:02.280
What? Richard?

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.340
Seigi...

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.020
You've grown so much!

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:08.280
Nakata-san?

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:09.600
You worked so hard!

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.160
I can't breathe...

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.450
Sorry I'm late!

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:32.160
How was your coming-of-age ceremony?

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.500
Everyone was surprised when they saw these.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.560
They suit you.

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:41.260
Nakata-sama made an excellent choice.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.970
He really is your father.

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:47.440
Richard, could you take a picture of me?

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:48.720
I want to send it to him.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:51.340
Very well.

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:01.800
Thanks.

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:05.610
Seigi, do you recall what tanzanite signifies?

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.120
Rebirth?

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.650
Good for you.

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:16.740
Let us celebrate today as the 
birth of the new Nakata Seigi.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.490
Even if I'm reborn, 
I want to stay Nakata Seigi.

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:27.260
I got to meet you, after all.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:34.420
Anyway, I thought I should gift 
you something, as well.

00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:36.480
So I'd like to teach you English.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:38.310
What? Where's this coming from?

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.760
Your English in London was atrocious.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:47.780
But I'd be really happy to have you teach me.

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:56.430
Seigi, make some tea.

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:57.380
You got it!
